>> Random numbers

  rand(lo, hi)
      A random int in [lo, hi] inclusive (raises if lo > hi).
  randf(lo, hi)
      A random float in [lo, hi] (raises if lo > hi or not finite).
>> Slices (copy-on-write)

var s = a[1:3];

A slice is a new array, separate from the one it was taken from - and, like any array, shared once you have it: assigning or passing it does not copy it again (Python's rule). Internally it is a cheap VIEW until written: a write through any name holding it copies the window once, for all of them. intptr(x) reveals when two values share storage.
